concept:treasury-laws-amendment-australian-consumer-law-review-act-2018-sch-9-sec-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 At the end of section 63 of Schedule 2"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-9-sec-2 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  (2) To avoid doubt, subsection (1)(a) does not apply if the consignee of the goods is not carrying on or engaged in a business, trade, profession or occupation in relation to the goods. Note: This subsection was inserted as a response to the decision of the High Court of Australia in Wallis v Downard-Pickford (North Queensland) Pty Ltd [1994] HCA 17.  Consumer protection  Schedule 10  No. 132, 2018 Treasury Laws Amendment (Australian Consumer Law Review) Act" ;
    skos:definition "Add:  (2) To avoid doubt, subsection (1)(a) does not apply if the consignee of the goods is not carrying on or engaged in a business, trade, profession or occupation in relation to the goods. Note: This subsection was inserted as a response to the decision of the High Court of Australia in Wallis v Downard-Pickford (North Queensland) Pty Ltd [1994] HCA 17.  Consumer protection  Schedule 10  No. 132, 2018 Treasury Laws Amendment (Australian Consumer Law Review) Act"@en ;
